In __init__, store each parameter on self, for example self.name = name.
Each method uses self to reach those attributes, like f"{self.name} says: Woof!".
birthday() adds 1 to self.age before printing the message.
dog_years() should return a value (age times 7), not print it.
__str__ must return a string; build it with an f-string.
For the stretch, a class variable is set once inside the class body, outside any method.
